\v 6 The¦371106 king¦371109 of Nineveh¦371111 also¦371112 heard about¦371109 it¦371112 and he¦371112 got¦371114 down¦371119 from¦371113 his throne¦371113, took¦371114 off¦371114 his robe¦371115 and put on¦371120 sackcloth¦371118, then¦371105 sat¦371119 in a pile of ashes¦371122.
\v 7 And¦371124 he¦371124 had¦371124 a statement written out and¦371125 publicly read throughout Nineveh¦371126, saying¦371125, “The¦371127 king¦371128 and¦371129 his¦371129 advisors declare that people¦371131 and¦371132 livestock¦371132, be it¦371125 herds¦371133 or flocks¦371134, are prohibited from grazing¦371141 or eating anything¦371138, and¦371142 even from drinking¦371145 water¦371142.
\v 8 Both people¦371149 and¦371150 livestock¦371150 should just wear sacks, and¦371151 they should use their¦371164 strength to cry¦371151 out¦371151 to¦371152 God¦371154 and¦371156 they should turn¦371156 away from¦371158 the¦371159 evil¦371159 and¦371160 violent¦371162 things they have been¦371164 doing.
