\v 2 And¦371215 he¦371215 said¦371215 to Yahweh, “Please¦371216 Yahweh, wasn't this¦371220 what I said would happen when I was¦371224 still in my¦371227 own¦371227 country¦371227? That's¦371236 why I fled¦371232 to¦371233 Tarshish¦371233 the¦371250 first¦371231 time¦371231, because¦371234 I knew¦371235 that¦371220 you¦371237 are¦371238 a caring forgiving god¦371238, who¦371247 doesn't get angry¦371243 quickly; full of¦371221 kindness¦371246 and¦371211 not¦371218 wanting to¦371232 cause distress.\x + \xo 4:2: \xt Exo 34:6.\x*
